  "about": "What lifts me (Plus, inside More patterns; specs/1.3-grounding-and-good-things.md part 2 and its rulings, UX & PM 14 Nov). TEMPORARY HOME: the Mobile Dev moves this to the app repo's supabase/contracts/what-lifts-me.json and owns it; the web then syncs it (decision 99). For each tag used on at least minDaysWith checked-in days of More patterns' period, with at least minDaysWithout checked-in days without it: the average mood on each side, each rounded to one decimal; the gap is a minus b, rounded. Shown: the max largest gaps of minGap or more, positive only, largest first (ties: the tag used on more days, then alphabetical). Never a negative framing, no advice, no AI. Computed on the fly from the person's own rows; never stored, cached or logged. Never shown, nor counted: a tag the S-03 crisis matcher flags (every language), or a tag matching exclude in ANY language. Matching: the tag is lower-cased (NFKC), diacritics stripped except for Thai, and split into words at anything that isn't a letter or a digit; a word that starts with one of a language's prefixes, or equals one of its words, excludes the tag. Thai has no spaces: its substrings match anywhere in the tag. The lists lean wide on purpose: a wrong match only hides a tag.",
